--
--
A mem-initializer naming an anonymous-union variant member
(`: __null_state_()`, [class.base.init]/2) is silently dropped from
the constructor (empty body; the member stays nondet).
check_member_initializers recognises the name (has_component_rec) and
full_member_initialization routes it, but the conversion loses it.
Blocks precise modelling of libc++ __optional_destruct_base
(cpp20_map_basic_libcxx's next layers).
Fixed 2026-08-03: the parser marks explicit empty initializers
("#value_init") and the anonymous-member path zero-initializes them
([dcl.init.general]/9); synthesized default-initialization entries
keep their indeterminate-value skip.
